{"url": "https://imprs-cpqm.mpg.de/101601/Admission", "final_url": "https://imprs-cpqm.mpg.de/101601/Admission", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-21", "text": "Admission | IMPRS-CPQM\nMain-Content\nAbout us\nIMPRS-CPQM\nMPI for Chemical Physics of Solids\nTU Dresden\nUniversity of St Andrews\nResearch partners\nMembers\nStudents\nManagement\nPrincipal Investigators\nAlumni\nDirections & Contact\nResearch & TRaining\nResearch activities\nPrincipal investigators\nPublications\nPhD research & training\nAvailable PhD projects\nSupervision\nApplication\nHow to apply\nApplication guidelines\nAvailable PhD projects\nOnline application\nSelection procedure\nAdditional information\nAdmission\nFinancial support\nFrequently Asked Questions\nNews Center\nNews from IMPRS-CPQM\nEvents\nCurrent events\nEvent archive\nInformation\nDirections & contact\nPractical information\nFrequently asked questions\nIMPRS-CPQM\nApplication\nAdmission\nAdmission to IMPRS-CPQM\nOnce you have been accepted as a new students in IMPRS-CPQM, you can rely on our full support in order to get a great start into your time in our program. Together with the Visitors' Program at MPI CPfS, we will make sure that you get all the help you need along the way. We will\nsupport you in the visa application procedure,\nprovide temporary housing for the time right after your arrival,\nhelp you with all the administrative requirements to obtain a residence permit,\nassist with the registration process at the university,\nand offer any other information or support you may need to have a smooth move and start.\nTop\nMax-Planck-Gesellschaft\nData Protection Advice\nImprint\n\u00a9\n2026, Max-Planck-Gesellschaft\n\u00a9 2003-2026, Max-Planck-Gesellschaft\nWeb-View\nPrint Page\nOpen in new window\nEstimated DIN-A4 page-width\nGo to Editor View", "links": [["Main-Content", "https://imprs-cpqm.mpg.de/101601/Admission#page_content"], ["", "https://imprs-cpqm.mpg.de/"], ["IMPRS-CPQM", "https://imprs-cpqm.mp